WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.065 --> 00:00:09.667
There once was a boy named Thomas who lived just down the street in the house with the

2
00:00:09.747 --> 00:00:10.407
red bricks.

3
00:00:10.887 --> 00:00:15.188
Thomas didn't care about the environment, and he never recycled his garbage.

4
00:00:16.268 --> 00:00:21.290
One day an old wizard smelled an awful stench while he was working in his basement.

5
00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:28.452
He walked upstairs and outside and kept following the scent until he found himself in front of Thomas'

6
00:00:28.492 --> 00:00:33.668
house. He stopped out front and looked at the garbage piled up on the curb.

7
00:00:33.968 --> 00:00:38.412
He shook his head with disgust and said, "Look at all this trash!

8
00:00:38.953 --> 00:00:42.416
Thomas must learn that he should not waste his garbage."

9
00:00:45.799 --> 00:00:49.543
The wizard pulled out his wand and put a spell on Thomas' house.

10
00:00:50.444 --> 00:00:54.568
Now, every time Thomas threw away good garbage, it would talk to him.

11
00:00:55.376 --> 00:00:59.498
The spell would not go away until Thomas stopped wasting his garbage.

12
00:01:00.259 --> 00:01:04.621
That night Thomas noticed a mistake after he printed his homework.

13
00:01:05.402 --> 00:01:08.403
Without thinking he threw the paper into the trash.

14
00:01:08.423 --> 00:01:11.125
"Hey! What are you doing?"

15
00:01:11.845 --> 00:01:12.526
said a voice.

16
00:01:12.546 --> 00:01:14.527
"Who said that?"

17
00:01:15.327 --> 00:01:16.128
Thomas asked.

18
00:01:17.208 --> 00:01:18.149
It was the paper!

19
00:01:18.169 --> 00:01:20.370
"You are wasting me!

20
00:01:21.271 --> 00:01:23.572
I am not garbage," it said.

21
00:01:24.496 --> 00:01:25.377
"Yes, you are!"

22
00:01:26.037 --> 00:01:26.857
Thomas pointed.

23
00:01:27.238 --> 00:01:29.099
"There is a mistake printed on you."

24
00:01:29.439 --> 00:01:29.999
"Look at me.

25
00:01:30.499 --> 00:01:33.141
I still have one blank side," said the paper.

26
00:01:33.161 --> 00:01:34.722
"What can I do with that?"

27
00:01:34.742 --> 00:01:36.323
"You could draw a picture.

28
00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:37.744
You could write a note.

29
00:01:38.204 --> 00:01:39.344
You could play a game.

30
00:01:39.745 --> 00:01:41.506
You could do your math homework."

31
00:01:42.226 --> 00:01:46.348
"Wow! I never thought about it before," said Thomas.

32
00:01:46.368 --> 00:01:49.670
"Well, you should start thinking about it more often.

33
00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:52.692
I am precious," the paper explained.

34
00:01:53.508 --> 00:01:55.429
"A tree had to die to make me.

35
00:01:55.989 --> 00:01:58.331
Don't waste a tree by throwing me away!

36
00:01:58.791 --> 00:02:00.132
You must learn to recycle."

37
00:02:00.832 --> 00:02:04.294
The next day Thomas went to the kitchen to make his lunch.

38
00:02:05.074 --> 00:02:08.436
He ate a peanut butter and jelly sandwich with a glass of milk.

39
00:02:08.976 --> 00:02:12.018
Then he put the empty peanut butter jar into the garbage.

40
00:02:12.678 --> 00:02:13.499
"Excuse me!

41
00:02:13.919 --> 00:02:15.600
Take me out of here right now!"

42
00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:17.001
said the jar.

43
00:02:17.021 --> 00:02:21.163
"Why? You're garbage," said Thomas.

44
00:02:21.183 --> 00:02:22.984
"No, I am not!

45
00:02:23.444 --> 00:02:25.246
You can use me for something else."

46
00:02:26.166 --> 00:02:26.967
"Something else?

47
00:02:27.507 --> 00:02:28.148
Like what?"

48
00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:30.290
"I can hold your marbles.

49
00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:31.991
I can hold your pennies.

50
00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:33.913
I can hold your candy.

51
00:02:34.553 --> 00:02:38.416
I can hold many small treasures," the jar answered.

52
00:02:39.237 --> 00:02:41.559
Thomas' head was spinning with ideas.

53
00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:45.342
This was the strangest thing that had ever happened to him.

54
00:02:46.023 --> 00:02:47.043
Talking garbage!

55
00:02:47.704 --> 00:02:52.288
But he agreed that the jar was very useful, so he put it in a safe place.

56
00:02:53.552 --> 00:02:58.794
Later that day, Thomas ate some oranges and threw the orange peels into the trash can.

57
00:02:59.395 --> 00:03:00.375
It happened again.

58
00:03:01.135 --> 00:03:03.116
This time the peels started to talk.

59
00:03:03.916 --> 00:03:06.197
"Stop! We do not belong in here."

60
00:03:06.217 --> 00:03:08.038
"Why not?

61
00:03:08.618 --> 00:03:10.379
You're definitely garbage!"

62
00:03:10.799 --> 00:03:11.499
said Thomas.

63
00:03:11.519 --> 00:03:14.941
"There is no way I can reuse you.

64
00:03:15.381 --> 00:03:16.562
You would smell bad."

65
00:03:16.582 --> 00:03:20.163
"No, we are very special garbage.

66
00:03:20.583 --> 00:03:23.496
We go into the compost bin," said the peels.

67
00:03:23.516 --> 00:03:25.457
"What is a compost bin?"

68
00:03:25.977 --> 00:03:26.637
asked Thomas.

69
00:03:26.657 --> 00:03:31.599
"A compost bin is a special box where you put all your vegetable and fruit scraps.

70
00:03:32.239 --> 00:03:36.520
In the spring, you put us into your garden, and we help your flowers grow."

71
00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:43.422
Thomas did not understand why his garbage was talking all of a sudden, but he started to understand

72
00:03:43.522 --> 00:03:44.422
what it was saying.

73
00:03:45.303 --> 00:03:49.684
He took the orange peels out of the trash can and put them into the compost bin.

74
00:03:50.576 --> 00:03:56.319
The next morning, while Thomas was getting dressed, he accidentally ripped his shirt as he pulled it over

75
00:03:56.379 --> 00:03:56.819
his head.

76
00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:01.442
Since it was an old shirt, he took it off and threw it into the garbage.

77
00:04:01.462 --> 00:04:03.423
"Where am I going?"

78
00:04:03.783 --> 00:04:04.504
asked the shirt.

79
00:04:05.304 --> 00:04:08.986
"You are an old ripped shirt, so you are going into the garbage.

80
00:04:09.506 --> 00:04:13.528
I'm sorry, but there is nothing I can do with you," said Thomas.

81
00:04:13.549 --> 00:04:15.389
"You are wrong, Thomas!

82
00:04:16.070 --> 00:04:17.851
You can use me as a rag.

83
00:04:18.411 --> 00:04:19.772
I can wash the floor.

84
00:04:20.344 --> 00:04:23.046
I can clean your bike," explained the shirt.

85
00:04:23.747 --> 00:04:24.988
Thomas was amazed.

86
00:04:25.528 --> 00:04:31.052
It seemed that everything that used to be garbage still had a job to do─even orange peels and

87
00:04:31.132 --> 00:04:31.893
ripped clothes!

88
00:04:32.313 --> 00:04:34.775
He had a whole new understanding of his trash.

89
00:04:35.196 --> 00:04:37.457
Thomas learned a lot from the talking garbage.

90
00:04:38.198 --> 00:04:41.100
He did not want to cause environmental problems anymore.

91
00:04:41.821 --> 00:04:45.804
That afternoon he went around the house and looked in all of the garbage bins.

92
00:04:46.496 --> 00:04:51.181
He found everything that he could reuse and put it all in a special place with the rest

93
00:04:51.221 --> 00:04:52.021
of his treasures.

94
00:04:53.082 --> 00:04:56.165
The next week Thomas' garbage bag was very small.

95
00:04:56.666 --> 00:04:59.668
Even the garbage man was impressed when he came to pick it up.

96
00:05:00.009 --> 00:05:05.293
Thomas had saved all of the used paper, all of the empty bottles, and all of his old

97
00:05:05.353 --> 00:05:09.798
clothes. He had even made compost out of his fruits and vegetables!

98
00:05:10.178 --> 00:05:12.180
There was hardly anything to throw away.

99
00:05:12.628 --> 00:05:17.729
However, the garbage man was not the only person who was amazed by Thomas' new habit.

100
00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:22.991
The old wizard had also seen the small bag of garbage on the curb that day.

101
00:05:23.371 --> 00:05:28.793
During the night, when everyone was asleep, he walked by Thomas' house enjoying the fresh air.

102
00:05:29.613 --> 00:05:32.073
He smiled and laughed as he looked toward the house.

103
00:05:32.093 --> 00:05:35.634
"Ha-ha! Thomas, you have learned your lesson.

104
00:05:35.914 --> 00:05:41.136
You have learned to save your garbage, so I will remove the spell from your house."
